    Add support for redirected VTL0 interrupts
    
    This code enables the changes made here: https://github.com/microsoft/openvmm/pull/384
    
    Implements tdx: https://github.com/microsoft/openvmm/issues/362
    
    Currently on TDX CVMs, VTL0 owned device interrupts are delivered via proxy interrupt mechanism (CVM exits to hypervisor, hypervisor posts interrupt to VTL2 and then VTL2 forwards to VTL0). This creates a performance overhead due to the CVM exit to hypervisor.
    
    This change introduces a proxy interrupt redirection capability to improve performance:
    a) VTL2 requests proxy interrupt redirection during Retarget Device Interrupt HC.
    b) Hypervisor will remap the interrupts with posted interrupts enabled.
    c) When interrupt arrives, it will be delivered directly to VTL2 by the hardware through posted interrupt mechanism, without requiring any exit to hypervisor.
    d) And VTL2 can forward it to VTL0 as it currently does.
    
    Hyper-V support for proxy interrupt redirect capability is exposed via proxy_interrupt_redirect_available (bit 34) in HvRegisterVsmCapabilities

